From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:41:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] [CUDA] Support SM120 MXFP4 block-scaled MMA

Add mma.sync.m16n8k64.kind::mxf4nvf4.block_scale.scale_vec::2X with UE8M0
scales, one per 32 K elements, for packed E2M1 operands. MXFP4 runs on the
same packed-E2M1 operand path as NVFP4. T.gemm_blockscaled and
T.mma_gemm_blockscaled select it when both operands are packed E2M1 and the
scale granularity is 32; granularity 16 keeps NVFP4.

A packed scale word covers two K64 atoms; the byte selector (0 or 2) picks
the atom's half. The compact K-major scale package and the static
four-block ping-pong remain NVFP4-only; MXFP4 uses row-major scale words.

Validated on GB10 (sm_121a): exact MXFP4 products, and the block-scaled
suites (212 tests) pass.
